{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\eng\\096.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "O Listening", "conf": 0.751, "box": [[265, 227], [517, 208], [521, 263], [270, 282]]}, {"text": "is this poem different from other poems?", "conf": 0.957, "box": [[426, 439], [1054, 373], [1058, 413], [430, 479]]}, {"text": "Stopping by Woods on a Snowy Evening", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[450, 552], [1221, 474], [1226, 524], [455, 601]]}, {"text": "Whosewoods these areI thinkIknow.", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[547, 638], [1133, 583], [1136, 616], [550, 671]]}, {"text": "His house is in the village though,", "conf": 0.916, "box": [[546, 680], [1058, 636], [1061, 673], [549, 717]]}, {"text": "He will not see me stopping here", "conf": 0.875, "box": [[544, 723], [1051, 681], [1055, 721], [547, 764]]}, {"text": "To watch his woods fill up with snow.", "conf": 0.936, "box": [[545, 768], [1110, 722], [1113, 759], [548, 804]]}, {"text": "Rhythm and rhyme", "conf": 0.922, "box": [[1365, 761], [1638, 774], [1637, 815], [1363, 801]]}, {"text": "makes the poem", "conf": 0.873, "box": [[1365, 804], [1608, 815], [1607, 852], [1364, 841]]}, {"text": "really interesting.", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[1363, 845], [1610, 855], [1609, 895], [1362, 885]]}, {"text": "My little horse must think it queer", "conf": 0.878, "box": [[545, 855], [1068, 814], [1071, 853], [548, 894]]}, {"text": "Try to read the", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[1365, 890], [1584, 893], [1583, 930], [1365, 927]]}, {"text": "To stop without a farmhouse near", "conf": 0.922, "box": [[543, 901], [1066, 860], [1068, 897], [546, 938]]}, {"text": "poem with rhythm", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[1363, 929], [1631, 936], [1630, 976], [1362, 970]]}, {"text": "Between the woods and frozen lake", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[545, 945], [1089, 904], [1092, 938], [548, 980]]}, {"text": "listening to it will", "conf": 0.898, "box": [[1365, 975], [1613, 978], [1613, 1011], [1364, 1008]]}, {"text": "The darkest evening of the year.", "conf": 0.947, "box": [[544, 987], [1033, 955], [1035, 994], [547, 1026]]}, {"text": "com/Emplovee", "conf": 0.864, "box": [[1624, 999], [1691, 999], [1693, 1586], [1626, 1587]]}, {"text": "also help.", "conf": 0.853, "box": [[1366, 1011], [1506, 1018], [1504, 1056], [1364, 1049]]}, {"text": "He gives his harness bells a shake", "conf": 0.878, "box": [[544, 1077], [1059, 1042], [1062, 1079], [547, 1115]]}, {"text": "To ask if there is some mistake.", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[545, 1121], [1018, 1092], [1020, 1126], [547, 1156]]}, {"text": "The only other sound's the sweep", "conf": 0.916, "box": [[543, 1163], [1059, 1134], [1061, 1174], [545, 1203]]}, {"text": "Of easy wind and downy flake.", "conf": 0.901, "box": [[543, 1208], [1007, 1182], [1009, 1223], [545, 1248]]}, {"text": "The woods are lovely, dark and deep.", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[544, 1296], [1110, 1271], [1111, 1307], [545, 1333]]}, {"text": "But I have promises to keep,", "conf": 0.902, "box": [[543, 1340], [975, 1321], [977, 1362], [544, 1380]]}, {"text": "And miles to go before I sleep,", "conf": 0.951, "box": [[542, 1385], [1011, 1367], [1013, 1406], [543, 1424]]}, {"text": "And miles to go before I sleep.", "conf": 0.932, "box": [[542, 1431], [1011, 1412], [1013, 1451], [543, 1470]]}, {"text": "(By: Robert Frost)", "conf": 0.841, "box": [[884, 1510], [1152, 1495], [1154, 1536], [887, 1550]]}, {"text": "About the Author:", "conf": 0.874, "box": [[248, 1615], [548, 1607], [549, 1641], [249, 1648]]}, {"text": "Robert Lee Frost was born in 1874, in America. He was a renowned American Poet of the 20\"", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[252, 1671], [1685, 1640], [1686, 1682], [253, 1714]]}, {"text": "Century. The majority of his work had been published in England as well as America. He is stil", "conf": 0.941, "box": [[252, 1722], [1687, 1690], [1688, 1732], [253, 1764]]}, {"text": "known for his work on nature and natural beauty.", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[251, 1767], [974, 1757], [974, 1800], [252, 1809]]}, {"text": "Discuss with a partner:", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[252, 1849], [622, 1847], [623, 1884], [252, 1886]]}, {"text": "a. What is the main idea of the poem, 'Stopping by Woods on a Snowy Evening'?", "conf": 0.906, "box": [[248, 1909], [1549, 1898], [1550, 1942], [249, 1952]]}, {"text": "b. Why do you think the poet wrote this poem?", "conf": 0.937, "box": [[251, 1962], [988, 1958], [988, 1998], [251, 2002]]}, {"text": "C.", "conf": 0.554, "box": [[257, 2021], [287, 2021], [287, 2047], [257, 2047]]}, {"text": "Who do you think this poem appeals to?", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[299, 2014], [923, 2011], [923, 2051], [299, 2054]]}, {"text": "d. Did you enjoy the poem? What was its impact on you?", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[252, 2063], [1139, 2067], [1139, 2107], [252, 2104]]}, {"text": "91", "conf": 0.658, "box": [[914, 2131], [968, 2131], [968, 2171], [914, 2171]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.82, "box": [[1310, 2175], [1599, 2167], [1600, 2203], [1311, 2212]]}]}